<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bundesrat (German Empire)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1867">1867</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Federal Council of the North German Confederation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bundesrat, or Federal Council, was the chamber representing the governments of the member states of the North German Confederation from 1867 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> from 1871. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> held the most votes and the chancellor presided. It approved laws with the elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> and held much executive and administrative power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bundesrat-german-empire.jpg" alt="Bundesrat (German Empire)" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Emil Doepler Vector: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wappen_Deutsches_Reich_-_Reichsadler_1889.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
